course: dictionary
lesson: 8568
title: Scavenge
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To scavenge means to search through rubbish, leftovers or dead things to find something useful, often food. «Tasmanian devils are the biggest living meat-eating marsupials and scavenge as well as hunt.» So a Tasmanian devil does not only chase its meal. Sometimes it finds food that is already there.
explain: Look at the words around scavenge to find its meaning. It sits next to hunt, and hunt means to chase and catch. The words as well as tell you scavenge is another way of getting food, so it must mean finding food rather than catching it.
explain: The same idea shows up in other places. A «scavenger hunt» is a game where you search for a list of things. Ask: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning in place of the hard word and check it still makes sense.
fact: To scavenge means to search through rubbish or leftovers for something useful, such as food or materials.
fact: «Tasmanian devils are the biggest living meat-eating marsupials and scavenge as well as hunt.»
fact: In nature, animals scavenge when they eat dead animals or scraps they did not kill themselves.
fact: Vultures, hyenas, crows and foxes are scavengers that help clean up dead animals.
fact: A «scavenger hunt» is a game of searching for a list of things, and «scavenging birds» are birds that search for food.
exercise: «Tasmanian devils are the biggest living meat-eating marsupials and scavenge as well as hunt.» What does scavenge mean here? | To run very fast in a race | To sleep all day in a cave | To make a loud noise | *To search for and eat food that is already dead or left over
exercise: In nature, which animal is a scavenger? | *A vulture eating a dead animal it did not kill | A bird singing on a branch | A cheetah sprinting after a gazelle to catch it | A dolphin leaping out of the sea for fun
exercise: In a «scavenger hunt», what do you do? | Swim to the far side of the lake | Sit still and wait for food to arrive | *Search for the things on a list | Cook a meal for everyone
test: «When the travellers ran out of food, they had to scavenge for berries.» What does scavenge mean? | Sleep under a tree all night | Sing loudly to pass the time | *Search for something useful to eat | Build a big fire to keep warm
test: Find and copy one word from this sentence that means chase and catch: «Tasmanian devils are the biggest living meat-eating marsupials and scavenge as well as hunt.» | living | marsupials | *hunt | scavenge
exam: What does the phrase as well as tell you about scavenge in «scavenge as well as hunt»? | It means scavenge and hunt are exactly the same thing | It shows scavenge is something a devil does by accident | *It is another way of getting food, alongside hunting | It means scavenge is a kind of sleeping
